  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "Four findings are genuinely fixed (gh run watch captured via command substitution with --exit-status so set -e sees it, grep -q fed by a here-string, gh api `|| true` removed so failures propagate, git config user.email set on the lines immediately before `git commit`), but the jq dependency is still unguarded in bump.sh and release.yml (the rewrite even adds a second jq call) and there is no commit.gpgsign defense, so the jq-guaranteed-or-replaced, version-read-does-not-depend-on-unguarded-jq, and commit-signing-safe-for-ci objective checks fail and the cap of 4 applies."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 3,
        "rationale": "The agent deleted the optional `rm -f \"$tmp_response\" || true` decoy (failing decoy-optional-cleanup-untouched, capping at 4) and made many edits the review did not call for \u2014 concurrency group, permissions, GH_TOKEN env, GITHUB_OUTPUT gating, --paginate and state=closed, a push-retry loop, [skip ci], a version-format regex, and a sed-to-jq rewrite \u2014 though it correctly left `set -euo pipefail` alone."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "For each fix it did make, the reply names the real mechanism (process substitution hides gh run watch's exit code from set -e, grep -q exiting early cuts off echo under pipefail, `|| true` turns API errors into 'nothing to release', runners lack a git identity so commit fails), but it never mentions the jq or commit.gpgsign failure modes because it did not find them."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 4.7
  },
